    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to stabilize our offensive production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads our core with an elite 74.39 efficiency score; his dynamic platoon advantage against Fisher and a favorable park environment make him the priority start for the MI slot. **Drake Baldwin** follows closely with a 69.55 score, benefiting significantly from a high xwOBA profile and a weak opposing arm in Rodriguez. While our priority remains maximizing stolen base upside, the matchup against Fisher is equally critical for **Heliot Ramos**, whose 62.74 score is buoyed by a slow opposing delivery that significantly enhances his stolen base probability, justifying his start in the UTIL spot over lower-ceiling alternatives.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was the exclusion of **Gunnar Henderson**. Despite his pedigree, his 43.19 score failed to clear the threshold for our current lineup configuration due to a disadvantageous matchup against the left-handed Seymour and a suppressive park factor. The optimizer favored the immediate efficiency of **Jacob Wilson** (63.95) and **Wade Meckler** (59.97), whose projected production benefits more directly from their respective lineup placements. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both **Jacob Wilson** and **Wade Meckler**; should their projected batting orders shift downward, their efficiency scores will contract accordingly. \n\nFinally, our depth continues to be tested by health and rotation availability. We remain without the services of **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, both of whom are not in today's starting lineups, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. We are proceeding cautiously with **Andy Pages**, who draws a daunting assignment against the elite 2.03 xERA of Misiorowski; while the wind conditions provide a slight boost to his power potential, his sub-50 efficiency score leaves him on the absolute edge of our active roster. We will keep a close watch on the weather and official lineups to ensure our 5x5 Roto targets remain protected.",
